; The output stage. The lattice's output f in; the de-emphasis yd = f + 0.9 yd, then the sample 20 yd out as two
; values, the thousands and then the units (0-999), as lubdub's decoder outputs them. yd is kept as thousands H and
; units L with yd's sign; 0.9 L is (9 L + 5 away from zero) / 10, except that when f is 0 it is 9 L / 10 truncated,
; so that in a pause yd dies away to 0 instead of sticking at up to 5, which rounding would hold forever. 2 yd is
; made first, its units summed on top of 2000 so they never go negative (STO keeps them as U, SFT 03 gives the
; carry); then 20 yd is 10 times that: its thousands are 10 T + U / 100 (SFT 10, SFT 02) and its units
; 10 (U mod 100) (SFT 21).
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            loop    INP   f        03-21: r = 0.9 L, rounded, or truncated when f is 0
  04                    CLA   f
  05                    TAC   rnd
  06                    CLA   z
  07                    SUB   f
  08                    TAC   rnd
  09                    CLA   lo
  10                    SFT   10
  11                    SUB   lo
  12                    JMP   sh
  13            rnd     CLA   lo
  14                    SFT   10
  15                    SUB   lo
  16                    TAC   neg
  17                    ADD   five
  18                    JMP   sh
  19            neg     SUB   five
  20            sh      SFT   01
  21                    STO   r
  22                    CLA   hi       22-30: yd = 900 H + r + f, into H and L
  23                    SFT   10
  24                    SUB   hi
  25                    SFT   20
  26                    ADD   r
  27                    ADD   f
  28                    STO   lo
  29                    SFT   03
  30                    STO   hi
  31                    CLA   two      31-51: 2 yd as T and U, then 20 yd
  32                    SFT   30
  33                    ADD   lo
  34                    ADD   lo
  35                    STO   u
  36                    SFT   03
  37                    ADD   hi
  38                    ADD   hi
  39                    SUB   two
  40                    SFT   10
  41                    STO   th
  42                    CLA   u
  43                    SFT   02
  44                    ADD   th
  45                    STO   th
  46                    CLA   u
  47                    SFT   21
  48                    STO   u
  49                    OUT   th
  50                    OUT   u
  51                    JMP   loop
  52            f       DATA  0
  53            lo      DATA  0
  54            hi      DATA  0
  55            r       DATA  0
  56            u       DATA  0
  57            th      DATA  0
  58            five    DATA  5
  59            two     DATA  2
  60            z       DATA  0
